DESCRIPTION:Location: Kluge-Ruhe Aboriginal Art Collection<br>Audience: 
 Undergraduate\,Graduate\,Professional Students\,Faculty & Staff\,Alumni
 \,Public<br>Event Type: Exhibit<br>Type of Event: Ongoing<br>Link: https:
 //kluge-ruhe.org/all-exhibitions/color-is-life-womens-work-today/<br><br
 >&#39\;Color is Life: Women&#8217\;s Work Today&#39\; is a celebration o
 f First Nations women artists from across Australia. The artists represe
 nted here have created bold works of art that vibrantly reflect their li
 ved experiences and living cultural practices. Artmaking has long been a
  life force for women and their communities. As the Tiwi artist Jean Bap
 tiste Apuatimi said\, &#8220\;Painting makes me alive.&#8221\; <br><br>T
 he artworks in this exhibition are all held in the Kluge-Ruhe collection
 \, except for the film &#39\;Kala Kunbolk&#39\; (2023)\, which is on loa
 n from Injalak Arts Centre. The exhibition is supported by UVA Arts.
CATEGORIES:kluge-ruhe
